.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_ATTRIBUTES 3 2026-09-10 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_attributes \- query the archive attributes presence mask
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_attributes("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s " "*mpq_archive",
.BI "        uint32_t      " "*flags"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Return the archive's (attributes) array-presence mask in \fIflags\fP:
CRC32 (1), FILETIME (2), MD5 (4), and PATCH_BIT (8). A successful zero
mask is distinct from an absent file. The output is zeroed on failure.
.PP
The query lazily loads (attributes) through ordinary MPQ file reading.
Its payload version is 100, independent of archive format v1 or v2.
Malformed optional metadata does not prevent opening or ordinary extraction;
it fails an explicit query. No patch application is performed.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns LIBMPQ_SUCCESS on success or a negative libmpq error.
LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST means the (attributes) file is absent;
LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT means malformed attributes.
I/O and allocation errors are propagated.
NULL arguments return EXIST. Use on the wrong handle type returns NOT_INITIALIZED.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_create_mpqe (3),
.BR libmpq__file_attributes (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_timestamp (3),
.BR libmpq__writer_finish (3)
